00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:24.820
List your first and second choice of electives in order.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:24.820
First choice:

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:27.570
I'm glad I was able to decide by myself.

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:31.530
Sae and Hiro were so helpful.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:38.980
Now that I think of it, I've been able to visualize my future since last fall.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:45.090
December
10th

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:45.090
"Because the
Cup Is Small"

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:48.090
New Books Corner

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:50.090
Clouds and Sky

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:50.090
"The sky is so wide, so big"

00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:52.850
What a wonderful album!

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:57.100
MSRP ¥6,800

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:57.100
○×Inc.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:57.100
But it's so expensive.

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:00.100
I'll just look around a little more and then go home.

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:07.990
I'm so clumsy.

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:13.740
Huh? Yuno?

00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:19.250
Make
Millions
with
Stocks!!

00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:19.250
The day-trader's
complete guide
that even a monkey
could understand

00:14:16.030 --> 00:14:18.050
You're buying that?

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:26.380
What did you come here for?

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:28.760
I came looking for materials.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:29.300
Take the train?

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:30.760
No, I walked.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:33.760
What were you looking for?

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:36.220
I just came to check out the new pulps.

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:40.350
And, well, an SAT book.

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:42.850
A book about babies?

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:46.020
No! One of these.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:47.860
Oh, it's a study guide.

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:51.110
Yeah, it's not a baby book.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:58.240
The magazine you write for goes on sale today, doesn't it?

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:05.000
This month is my first novella, but it looks like they don't carry it.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:08.500
I'll ask someone who works here.

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:10.870
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:16.510
For some reason, this month's was really popular. We're already sold out.

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:13.680
College Exam Series

00:15:16.510 --> 00:15:18.300
I see.

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:21.520
I can ring you up now.

00:15:23.510 --> 00:15:25.000
You can keep the change.

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:26.770
I'm sorry, I can't!

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:33.820
Monthly
KIRARA

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:33.820
Jan

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:37.480
I have to wait until I get home. I have to wait.

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:43.870
Hey, Yuno, want to get a drink?

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:44.540
Sure.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:46.790
Welcome!

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:49.800
I like this place.

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:51.710
It's really fancy.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:55.400
I usually only get to come here for meetings.

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:58.570
The little decorations are so cute.

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:00.310
It has a nice atmosphere.

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:04.140
The cushions are really puffy too.

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:07.190
Hey, do you hear something?

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:11.690
I'm sorry! Are you okay?

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:15.850
Sorry!

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:18.700
It's okay. Can I have a blend?

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:20.450
How about you?

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:22.450
Um, um...

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:24.970
An espresso.

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:26.450
I'll have it right out.

00:16:30.310 --> 00:16:32.590
I'm not used to this. It's embarrassing.

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:34.970
Don't worry about it so much.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:42.470
Here's your espresso,

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:44.980
and here's your blend.

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:53.490
Um... Is it supposed to match my size?

00:16:57.070 --> 00:17:01.990
Espresso is a lot more bitter than normal coffee.

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.750
Don't force yourself.

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:05.870
Sae, aren't you using any sugar?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:10.000
I drink mine black.

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:12.750
I always use two.

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:15.130
You're so mature.

00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:23.350
That study guide you bought is for a literary program, right?

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:26.230
Are you going to go to a lit school?

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.280
Oh, um...

00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:34.150
Actually, I'm not sure whether to go for literature or art.

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:37.490
I know I should've made up my mind by now, but...

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:40.850
It's sweet! Too sweet!

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.830
You're right.

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:45.750
I forgot how small the cup was!

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:56.260
I know I should study literature, since that's what I want as a career.

00:17:56.620 --> 00:18:02.350
But these past two years at Yamabuki have really turned me on to art.

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:07.270
I only started it to illustrate my own work, so I don't want it to take over completely, but...

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:14.270
I know taking them both halfway isn't any good, but I still want to pick both.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:17.780
Sorry, I'm just rambling.

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:24.530
Don't worry! They say a bird in the hand is better than two in the bush!

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:30.250
That was great, thanks.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:31.620
You're welcome.

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:40.310
Why's she there that late?

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:42.260
Club or exams, I guess?

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:47.490
Oh, you talked with Sae about that?

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:50.270
Yeah. I never realized.

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:55.150
We're both indecisive. Sae knows what she wants, but isn't sure what to go for.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:59.900
I don't even know what I want. It's completely different.

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:02.450
She really is older.

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:03.700
Yeah.

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.370
How about you?

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:08.750
Me? I've decided on two things.

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:09.660
Really?

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:13.510
"I'm not gonna think about it," and "que sera sera."

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:15.170
You're amazing, Miya.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:21.320
You talked with Yuno about that?

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:24.680
Yeah, it turned out that way.

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:30.180
I tried to act like a big sister, but I just ended up showing her how pathetic I am.

00:19:30.180 --> 00:19:35.440
You're not pathetic! You're worried about an important and wonderful decision!

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:38.440
I think Yuno feels the same way.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.360
I'll make some coffee.

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.200
Thanks.

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:46.700
You use two sugars, right?

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.180
Yeah, and milk.

00:19:48.180 --> 00:19:50.490
Okay, the usual.

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:15.130
Espresso...

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:17.730
Maybe I'll be able to drink it when I grow up?

00:20:19.430 --> 00:20:23.860
Or maybe being able to drink it will mean I've grown up?

00:20:33.010 --> 00:20:36.120
It's still so bitter.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:40.040
December 10th

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:40.040
The end

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:40.040
To be continued

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:43.440
What a cute cushion!

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:46.320
Isn't it nice? I got it at the hundred yen shop.

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:50.180
They've had a lot of wonderful things lately.

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:52.900
Yeah, I go there to buy stationery sometimes.

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:55.600
But a hundred yen is still just a hundred yen.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:21:02.320
What do I do?
It's gotten
so quiet...
I'm the
oldest one.
I have to do
something.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:21:02.320
Um... Um...
I know.
This always
works in
girls'
comics...

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:58.560
They don't sell curtains or anything big.

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:00.700
Curtains!?

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:05.040
Next time, "April 15th: Satisfying Sunlight."

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:08.820
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments. Be sure to come see us!
